cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RSA-Porous2D in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "RSA-Porous2D: an open-source generator of two-dimensional polydisperse circular-grain porous media for pore-scale CFD and CFD-DEM simulation"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-06-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Fuadqr/RSA-Porous2D"
abstract: "RSA-Porous2D is an open-source Python tool for generating reproducible two-dimensional porous media composed of polydisperse circular grains. It supports controlled grain-size distributions, porosity targets, pore-throat controls, heterogeneous regions, automatic pore-throat analysis, solver-ready exports, and an optional PySide6 graphical user interface."
keywords:
  - random sequential adsorption
  - porous media
  - pore-scale modelling
  - CFD-DEM
  - throat analysis
  - Python
